THIRUVANANTHAPURAM, India,, August 27 (IPS)  - India is ranked the second-largest fish-producing nation globally, accounting for around 8 percent of global output. The fisheries sector in India accounts for nearly 7.43 percent of Agricultural Gross Value Added (GVA), the highest (independent) share among the agriculture and allied sectors.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43909&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Fishers’ Organisations in India Demand Recognition From FAO”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43917</id><title>Aid reaches hundreds of thousands in Gaza amid severe food insecurity</title><updated>2026-08-27T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43917" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;As hunger deepens across Gaza, humanitarian agencies continue to deliver food and other essential supplies to families in need.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43917&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Aid reaches hundreds of thousands in Gaza amid severe food insecurity”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43916</id><title>After Israeli seizure of Kalandia training centre, UNRWA warns of impact on youth</title><updated>2026-08-27T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43916" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/20-02-2025_UNRWA_Kalandia_Center.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/20-02-2025_UNRWA_Kalandia_Center.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/20-02-2025_UNRWA_Kalandia_Center.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/20-02-2025_UNRWA_Kalandia_Center.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The seizure of a vocational training centre in occupied East Jerusalem has left hundreds of Palestinian young people without access to skills and training that could help shape their futures. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43916&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “After Israeli seizure of Kalandia training centre, UNRWA warns of impact on youth”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43915</id><title>UN chief condemns “indifference” as Ebola cases mount in DR Congo</title><updated>2026-08-27T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43915" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/24-08-2026-UNFPA-DRC-Ebola-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/24-08-2026-UNFPA-DRC-Ebola-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/24-08-2026-UNFPA-DRC-Ebola-01.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/24-08-2026-UNFPA-DRC-Ebola-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Ebola Bundibugyo outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) requires “urgent” action and funding to rein in its alarming spread, the UN Secretary-General told reporters at UN Headquarters on Thursday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43915&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UN chief condemns “indifference” as Ebola cases mount in DR Congo”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43914</id><title>Lebanon: Civilian risks grow as military activity continues, UN says</title><updated>2026-08-27T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43914" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;Damaged roads, disrupted services and ongoing military activity continue to put civilians at risk in south Lebanon as strikes between Israeli forces and Hezbollah continue, according to the UN’s peacekeeping mission in the country (UNIFIL).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43914&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Lebanon: Civilian risks grow as military activity continues, UN says”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43912</id><title>Security Council LIVE: Tracking Syria’s transition</title><updated>2026-08-27T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43912" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;As Damascus continues to rebuild after more than a decade of war – from the recent dissolution of the Kurdish-led Syrian Democratic Forces to the United States’ removal of Syria from its sponsors of terrorism list – a top UN official warned the Security Council on Thursday that international support can help tackle outstanding challenges. UN News app users can follow here.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43912&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Security Council LIVE: Tracking Syria’s transition”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43911</id><title>Shock and devastation remain, a day after Himalayan flood disaster</title><updated>2026-08-27T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43911" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;Amid reports that hundreds of people are still missing in Nepal and China after a floodwater surge slammed into towns and villages on Wednesday, aid teams have been working to reach communities cut off by the disaster.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43911&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Shock and devastation remain, a day after Himalayan flood disaster”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43908</id><title>UN Secretary General Expresses Sadness Over Lives Lost in Nepal-Tibet Flash Floods</title><updated>2026-08-27T04:32:56-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43908" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/UN0914644.webp" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/UN0914644.webp" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/UN0914644.webp" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/UN0914644.webp&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
KATHMANDU, August 27 (IPS)  - A massive geophysical disaster along the mountainous Nepal-Tibet border has left at least 160 people dead and hundreds more missing after a glacial collapse triggered devastating flash floods and mudslides on Wednesday.
